From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rumisle <why-excuse-quail@duck.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:49:00 +0800
Subject: core/session: notices from plugins in the transcript
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A new transcript message type, notice ({source, level: info|warning, text}), that is never
sent to the model and never compacted, like the model and agent switch markers. Plugins
post one with ctx.session.notice (HTTP: POST /api/session/:id/notice) and get its id back;
posting again with that id replaces the notice in place. A notice may carry usage
({cost, tokens}), which counts toward the session's cost and tokens like
session.usage.recorded (pi's usage entries for cache warming work the same way).

First user: opencode-cache-warmer ("Cache kept warm · 3 refreshes · $0.09", and
"Cache miss after 7m idle · 150k tokens re-billed · ~$0.72" as a warning).

Client types and openapi.json are regenerated (openapi.json was already stale).

Ocelot-Patch: core/session-notices

